"""The Meridian series: one arc per module, written here and built into data/story/<mid>.json by tools/story/build.py.
The bible is qa/design/STORY.md. Each arc frames real work and never replaces it: every scene's link in `to` opens the
lesson, lab, exercise, F7 step, simulator challenge, design problem or quiz it leads into.

Per module:
  season      1 to 5
  arc         the module's story in about 120 words
  scenes      monday (the stakeholder's problem), midweek (the incident), friday (the fix you ship); finale on the
              last module of a season (the weekend boss round); each at most 60 words, second person, light tone
  to          the in-app link each scene opens
  previously  one line per day of the module (about 20 words): recalls yesterday as a question, never a recap
  cliff       one line per day: an open question that the next day's real content answers
Days are the module's plan days in order; a reader uses index min(day, len - 1)."""

SEASONS = {
    1: ('Foundations', 'You join Meridian and earn the right to change things: clean Python, honest numbers and a model everyone can use.'),
    2: ('The Platform', 'You build the platform Meridian runs on, from the first event to the source of truth, and keep it standing.'),
    3: ('Scale and Cloud', 'Meridian grows past one region and one bill; you move it to the cloud and design for ten times the traffic.'),
    4: ('AI at Meridian', 'Agents, retrieval and model features arrive; you make them useful, measured, cheap enough and safe.'),
    5: ('Lead', 'The work becomes people, money and direction: data products, governance, a blueprint and a promotion case.'),
}

